«
@@ ============================================================
@@ NACA4 — zero lift angle, lift and moment of a NACA 4-digit
@@ airfoil, by thin airfoil theory.
@@
@@ Input:  the digits of the airfoil as a number, such as 2415, or
@@         12 for a NACA 0012, and the angle of attack: a value with
@@         an angle unit, or a plain number of degrees.
@@ Output: α0, the zero lift angle, in degrees; Cl, the lift
@@         coefficient; Cm4 and CmLE, the moment coefficients about
@@         the quarter chord and the leading edge; tagged.
@@ Method: the first digit gives the maximum camber m in % of the
@@ chord, the second its position p in tenths. The camber line of
@@ two parabolas joined at p has a slope that is integrated in closed
@@ form with x = (1 − cos θ)/2. The thickness, the last two digits,
@@ plays no part in this theory.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================
  → nac aoa
  «
    IF nac 0 < nac 9999 > OR THEN
      "NACA4 needs the 4 digits of an airfoil, such as 2415" DoError
    END
    nac 1000 / IP →Num 100 /
    nac 100 / IP 10 MOD →Num 10 /
    → mc pc
    «
      IF mc 0 > pc 0 = AND THEN
        "NACA4: a cambered airfoil needs its second digit" DoError
      END
      'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
      RAD NoAngleUnits
      Ⓒπ →Num
      aoa IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_r CONVERT UVAL →Num ELSE →Num 180 / Ⓒπ →Num * END
      → amode aunits pic alr
      «
        IF mc 0 > THEN
          1 2 pc * - ACOS
          2 mc * pc SQ /
          2 mc * 1 pc - SQ /
          pc 0.5 -
          → tht k1p k2p qp
          «
            qp tht * tht SIN 2 / +
            qp tht SIN * tht 2 / 2 tht * SIN 4 / + 2 / +
            qp 2 tht * SIN * 2 / tht SIN 2 / 3 tht * SIN 6 / + 2 / +
            → i0c i1c i2c
            «
              k1p i0c * k2p qp pic * i0c - * +
              k1p i1c * k2p pic 4 / i1c - * +
              k1p k2p - i2c *
            »
          »
        ELSE
          0 0 0
        END
        → j0c j1c j2c
        «
          j0c j1c - pic /
          j2c j1c - 2 /
          → azr cm4c
          «
            2 pic * alr azr - *
            → clc
            «
              azr 180 * pic / 1_° * "α0" →TAG
              clc "Cl" →TAG
              cm4c "Cm4" →TAG
              cm4c clc 4 / - "CmLE" →TAG
            »
          »
        »
        amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
      »
    »
  »
»
